Changes in version 0.99.1
-------------------------

* Fit beta cosinor models using PQL with working-Gaussian maximum likelihood.
* Test rhythmicity with a null-model score test and estimate parameters from
  a separate full model. Support fixed-effects and random-intercept models,
  adjustment covariates, and an empirical Bayes prior on log precision.
* Return 13 result columns and retain design, EB prior, and fit summaries
  in metadata. Process CpGs in batches through BiocParallel.
* Classify parameter boundaries using the final undamped optimizer candidate.
* Plot marginal mean curves over the observed time range using saved fitting
  settings. Order panels by the selected CpGs.
* Add an evaluated workflow vignette and document the simulated example data.
* Maintain function documentation and exports with roxygen2, as in the
  original RhyME package.
* Shorten function help and default to MulticoreParam() for parallel fitting.
* Simplify plotting arguments to se, cpgs, and ncol; use a fixed curve grid.
* Remove topCpGs(); inspect and sort results directly from rowData().
* Assemble per-CpG results inside .fitOneCpG(), preserving partial fits.
* Keep compact workflow tests; archive development experiments separately.
* Document example data in the vignette and generation script.
* Use a short RUnit workflow test under inst/unitTests, following mist.
* Include 10,000 simulated CpGs using real-data-derived parameters and a
  serial EB workflow in the vignette.
